  "extra_setup": "Head also needs original deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash shards 47+48 + index + config.json (~190 GiB, native FP8 Engram tables) mounted at /engram-src. Worker gets weights via NFSv4 export from head (default WEIGHT_SYNC=nfs; zfs/rsync alternatives). CX7 RoCE link with per-node NIC/HCA pins (head enp1s0f1np1/rocep1s0f1, worker enp1s0f0np0/rocep1s0f0). start.sh bind-mounts ~16 overlay patch files into /opt/dsv41 and runs them before vllm serve; runs a GPU self-check container first. Optional ./start.sh pack writes per-rank Engram shards to local NVMe (+25-50% prefill).",
  "notes": "Per-node values: NODE_RANK 0 on head, 1 on worker (worker also passes --headless); CX7_IF/CX7_IB/NODE_IP per node; HEAD_IP=10.0.0.1. Do not pass --kv-cache-dtype (vLLM picks fp8_ds_mla). KV pool pinned at 2.5 GiB (774,400 tokens). MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS must be >=1536 with vision on. start.sh defaults differ from .env.example (e.g. EXL3_FAT_GROUPED=0, EXL3_TEMP_ROWS_FUSED=256 in script vs 1/16 in .env); values here follow .env.example, which start.sh copies to .env on first run. Engram tables come from the original checkpoint, not the EXL3 repo. Weights MIT (DeepSeek); launcher AGPL-3.0 with some MIT files.",
